From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: Activity Monitor counts guest RAM once (QEMU remaps its own view)

Applies after qemu-hvf-free-page-reclaim-reusable.patch.

What: a sweep remaps QEMU's own view of the VM's main RAM over itself
(mach_vm_remap, copy=FALSE, VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE), one
128 MB chunk at a time under the BQL, 20 ms apart; a pass a minute after
the start, then every 5 minutes, skipped while QEMU's footprint grew less
than 64 MB since the last pass, at most twice in a row (free page reports
can shrink the footprint while QEMU's touches grow it). The remap keeps the same VM objects at the
same offsets and drops only QEMU's page table entries; no page is touched,
copied or moved. Main RAM only, QEMU's private anonymous memory:
omacvm_ram_private(), which hvf_report_free_pages() now goes by too
(never the Venus host memory window's blobs, pflash, ROM, shared or
file-backed memory, nor while dirty logging is on). Before each remap
every map entry of the chunk must share its object with the hypervisor's
map (true shared or shared, an object id), be readable and writable and
not wired; else the chunk stays as it is and is counted (one qemu.log
line). In the first pass QEMU reads the chunk's objects and offsets again
after each remap: a change means QEMU's view is no longer the guest's
memory, and QEMU stops (abort) before it reads or writes there. A failed
remap that left the view as it was stops the sweep for the run (one line).
OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0 turns it off; a number of seconds sets the time
between passes (tests). qemu.log: a start line ("own-view sweep: on" or
"off": omacvm check's "Activity Monitor" row picks its words from it), a
line an hour from the sweep's own timer and one at exit (passes, passes
skipped, chunks remapped, MB less in Activity Monitor, the main lock's
hold per chunk: p99 and longest, chunks left as they were, why it
stopped); OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK=1 (tests) a line per pass.

Why: macOS charges a page to a process's footprint once for every mapping
that touched it, resident or compressed. A guest page counts through the
hypervisor's map when the guest touches it, and again through QEMU's own
mapping once QEMU's threads did (disk reads into guest RAM, network,
graphics transfers): no memory, but Activity Monitor shows it. A 4 GB VM
on a Mac mini showed 2.1 GB more after its boot and 2.5 GB of reads; a
12 GB VM on a MacBook Pro M1 Max 1.2-2.0 GB more with nothing compressed
(work/tracks/vm-memory.md). A page only QEMU touched since the guest last
did leaves the count until one of them touches it again: the Mac still
holds it (ADR 0066).

Upstream: OmacVM only (macOS accounting; upstream QEMU has no such sweep).
Test: Tests/memory/test-dcount.sh, no VM: guest RAM shared with a second
map or a real hv_vm_map; QEMU writes 1 GB, the guest reads it: the
footprint is 2.0x what the Mac holds; after one clean pass 1.001x (main,
without the sweep: 2.0x, the test fails); pass 1 runs while a thread
preads and pwrites a file into and out of guest RAM (buffered and
F_NOCACHE) and with two free page reports between chunks whose moves aside
are released after the pass; every page right as the guest sees it, and
QEMU's writes seen by the guest and the guest's by QEMU after it, the
replaced ranges too; an idle pass skipped, twice in a row at most; a chunk
with a copy-on-write entry or one without an object left as it is; a
failed remap stops the sweep; --predicate: which RAM blocks are swept;
--diverge: QEMU stops. The runtime build runs it on the patched source, CI
on this file.

diff --git a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
index 8f450f29..ef7a0752 100644
--- a/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
+++ b/accel/hvf/hvf-all.c
@@ -722,11 +722,473 @@ void hvf_report_free_pages_done(void)
 }
 /* omacvm-reclaim: end */
 
+/* omacvm-sweep: begin (app/runtime/Tests/memory/test-dcount.sh builds this part alone) */
+/*
+ * QEMU's own view of guest RAM, counted once (ADR 0066).
+ *
+ * macOS charges a page to a process's footprint (Activity Monitor's Memory)
+ * once for every mapping that touched it, resident or compressed: through
+ * the hypervisor's map when the guest touches it, and again through QEMU's
+ * own mapping once QEMU's threads did (disk reads into guest RAM, network,
+ * graphics transfers). Both mappings share the same VM objects (hv_vm_map
+ * makes them true shared), so the second count is no memory, but Activity
+ * Monitor shows it: a 4 GB VM showed 2.1 GB more after its boot and 2.5 GB
+ * of reads, and a compressed page keeps it until QEMU's mapping goes.
+ *
+ * The sweep remaps QEMU's view over itself (mach_vm_remap, copy=FALSE,
+ * VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE): the same objects at the same
+ * offsets, without QEMU's page table entries, so their charges go. No page
+ * is touched, copied or moved; QEMU's next touch maps a page again (about
+ * 0.4 us per 16 KiB page). A page only QEMU touched since the guest last
+ * did (a disk read the guest has not used yet) leaves the count until one
+ * of them touches it again; the Mac still holds it.
+ *
+ * Main RAM only, QEMU's private anonymous memory (omacvm_ram_private(), the
+ * rule a free page report goes by too), one 128 MB chunk (XNU's anonymous
+ * object) at a time under the BQL, 20 ms apart: a chunk never meets a free
+ * page report's replacement or its move aside, which run under the BQL too.
+ * A pass a minute after the start, then every 5 minutes, skipped while the
+ * footprint grew less than 64 MB since the last one, at most twice in a row
+ * (an idle VM; free page reports can shrink the footprint while QEMU's
+ * touches grow it, so at least every 15 minutes).
+ * Before each remap every map entry of the chunk must share its object
+ * (true shared or shared, an object id), be readable and writable and not
+ * wired: a remap of anything else (copy-on-write, or no object yet) gives
+ * QEMU's view memory of its own, and QEMU and the guest would no longer see
+ * the same pages. Such a chunk stays as it is and is counted (one qemu.log
+ * line). In the first pass the objects and offsets are read again after each
+ * remap: a change means that has happened anyway, and QEMU stops before it
+ * writes there. A failed remap that left the view as it was stops the sweep
+ * for the run (one line). OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP=0 turns it off; a number of
+ * seconds sets the time between passes (tests). qemu.log: the start line,
+ * a line an hour and one at exit (passes, MB less in Activity Monitor, the
+ * main lock's hold per chunk); OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK=1 (tests) a line
+ * per pass.
+ */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK (128ull << 20)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_GAP_NS (20 * 1000000LL)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_FIRST_S 60
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S 300
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_GROWTH (64ull << 20)
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_SKIPS 2              /* passes skipped in a row at most */
+#define OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS 8193            /* a chunk's 16 KiB pages, each its own object, and one */
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's own private anonymous guest RAM: what a free page report may
+ * replace and the sweep may remap. Never shared, file-backed, device, ROM or
+ * flash memory, nor memory QEMU was given rather than allocated
+ * (RAM_PREALLOC: memory_region_init_ram_ptr, as the Venus host memory
+ * window's blobs), nor while dirty logging write-protects it.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_ram_private(MemoryRegion *mr)
+{
+    RAMBlock *rb = mr->ram_block;
+
+    return memory_region_is_ram(mr) && !mr->readonly && !mr->rom_device &&
+           !memory_region_is_ram_device(mr) && rb && rb->fd < 0 &&
+           !(rb->flags & (RAM_SHARED | RAM_PREALLOC)) &&
+           !memory_region_get_dirty_log_mask(mr);
+}
+
+/* A piece of QEMU's view: one object, from an offset on. */
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepRun {
+    mach_vm_address_t start, end;
+    uint64_t object, offset;
+} OmacvmSweepRun;
+
+typedef struct OmacvmSweepStats {
+    uint64_t passes, idle, chunks, less, left, left_bytes;
+    int64_t longest_ns;
+    uint32_t hold[OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS];  /* per chunk, in the reclaim's 0.1 ms steps */
+} OmacvmSweepStats;
+
+typedef struct OmacvmSweep {
+    uint8_t *host;                      /* main RAM in QEMU's view */
+    uint64_t size;
+    int64_t period_ns, next_ns;         /* between passes; until the next step */
+    uint64_t at;                        /* the next chunk; size: between passes */
+    bool first, stopped, said_left, check;
+    unsigned skipped;                   /* passes skipped since the last one */
+    uint64_t footprint_after;           /* at the end of the last pass (0: none yet) */
+    int64_t hour_start;
+    char why[200];                      /* why it stopped */
+    OmacvmSweepStats hour, run;
+} OmacvmSweep;
+
+/* A chunk's pieces before a remap, and after it in the first pass. */
+static OmacvmSweepRun omacvm_sweep_runs[OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS], omacvm_sweep_after[OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS];
+
+/* OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP: unset: on, every 5 minutes; "0": off; 10-86400: seconds between passes (tests). */
+static int64_t omacvm_sweep_period(const char *v)
+{
+    char *end;
+    long s;
+
+    if (!v || !*v) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S;
+    }
+    s = strtol(v, &end, 10);
+    if (*end || s < 0) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_PERIOD_S;
+    }
+    if (s == 0) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return s < 10 ? 10 : s > 86400 ? 86400 : s;
+}
+
+static uint64_t omacvm_sweep_footprint(void)
+{
+    task_vm_info_data_t ti;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t n = TASK_VM_INFO_COUNT;
+
+    if (task_info(mach_task_self(), TASK_VM_INFO, (task_info_t)&ti, &n) != KERN_SUCCESS) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return ti.phys_footprint;
+}
+
+/*
+ * QEMU's view of [at, at + len): may a remap over itself keep it the
+ * guest's memory? Every map entry shares its object (true shared or shared,
+ * an object id), is readable and writable, not wired and inherited alike.
+ * Fills runs[] (*n of them, up to OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS; one object's adjacent
+ * pieces as one) and *inherit. Returns true, or false with the reason in why.
+ */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_entries(mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len,
+                                 OmacvmSweepRun *runs, unsigned *n,
+                                 vm_inherit_t *inherit, char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t a = at, end = at + len;
+    vm_region_submap_info_data_64_t info;
+    mach_msg_type_number_t count;
+    mach_vm_address_t start;
+    mach_vm_size_t size;
+    natural_t depth;
+    uint64_t offset;
+    OmacvmSweepRun *r;
+
+    *n = 0;
+    while (a < end) {
+        start = a;
+        size = 0;
+        depth = 0;
+        count = VM_REGION_SUBMAP_INFO_COUNT_64;
+        if (mach_vm_region_recurse(mach_task_self(), &start, &size, &depth,
+                                   (vm_region_recurse_info_t)&info, &count) != KERN_SUCCESS ||
+            start > a) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "nothing mapped at +%llu MB",
+                     (unsigned long long)((a - at) >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+        if (info.is_submap ||
+            (info.share_mode != SM_TRUESHARED && info.share_mode != SM_SHARED) ||
+            !info.object_id ||
+            (info.protection & (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE)) != (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE) ||
+            info.user_wired_count) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "a map entry at +%llu MB is not shared with the "
+                     "guest as QEMU's view must be (share mode %d, %s, protection %d, "
+                     "%s)", (unsigned long long)((a - at) >> 20), info.share_mode,
+                     info.object_id ? "an object" : "no object", info.protection,
+                     info.user_wired_count ? "wired" : "not wired");
+            return false;
+        }
+        if (a == at) {
+            *inherit = info.inheritance;
+        } else if (info.inheritance != *inherit) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "its map entries are inherited differently");
+            return false;
+        }
+        offset = info.offset + (a - start);
+        size = MIN(start + size, end) - a;
+        r = *n ? &runs[*n - 1] : NULL;
+        if (r && r->object == info.object_id && r->end == a &&
+            r->offset + (r->end - r->start) == offset) {
+            r->end = a + size;
+        } else if (*n == OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "more than %d map entries", OMACVM_SWEEP_RUNS);
+            return false;
+        } else {
+            runs[(*n)++] = (OmacvmSweepRun) { a, a + size, info.object_id, offset };
+        }
+        a += size;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/* After a remap: does QEMU's view of the chunk still map exactly runs[]? */
+static bool omacvm_sweep_same(mach_vm_address_t at, mach_vm_size_t len,
+                              const OmacvmSweepRun *runs, unsigned n,
+                              char *why, size_t whylen)
+{
+    const OmacvmSweepRun *b, *c;
+    vm_inherit_t inherit;
+    unsigned m, i;
+
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_entries(at, len, omacvm_sweep_after, &m, &inherit, why, whylen)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (m != n) {
+        snprintf(why, whylen, "%u pieces before, %u after", n, m);
+        return false;
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        b = &runs[i];
+        c = &omacvm_sweep_after[i];
+        if (b->start != c->start || b->end != c->end || b->object != c->object ||
+            b->offset != c->offset) {
+            snprintf(why, whylen, "another object or offset at +%llu MB",
+                     (unsigned long long)((c->start - at) >> 20));
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_add_hold(OmacvmSweep *s, int64_t ns)
+{
+    int step = MIN(ns / OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS, OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1);
+
+    s->hour.hold[step]++;
+    s->run.hold[step]++;
+    s->hour.longest_ns = MAX(s->hour.longest_ns, ns);
+    s->run.longest_ns = MAX(s->run.longest_ns, ns);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_stop(OmacvmSweep *s, const char *why)
+{
+    s->stopped = true;
+    snprintf(s->why, sizeof(s->why), "%s", why);
+    warn_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: stopped for this run: %s; Activity Monitor "
+                "counts the VM's pages QEMU touches twice again, as up to 3.2.16", why);
+}
+
+/* One chunk, under the BQL: check, remap, and in the first pass check again. */
+static void omacvm_sweep_chunk(OmacvmSweep *s)
+{
+    mach_vm_address_t at = (mach_vm_address_t)(uintptr_t)s->host + s->at, to = at;
+    mach_vm_size_t len = MIN(OMACVM_SWEEP_CHUNK, s->size - s->at);
+    int64_t start = get_clock();
+    vm_inherit_t inherit = VM_INHERIT_DEFAULT;
+    uint64_t before, after;
+    vm_prot_t cur, max;
+    kern_return_t kr;
+    char why[160], stop[200];
+    unsigned n;
+
+    s->at += len;
+    if (!omacvm_sweep_entries(at, len, omacvm_sweep_runs, &n, &inherit, why, sizeof(why))) {
+        s->hour.left++;
+        s->run.left++;
+        s->hour.left_bytes += len;
+        s->run.left_bytes += len;
+        if (!s->said_left) {
+            s->said_left = true;
+            warn_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: a chunk at +%llu MB stays as it is "
+                        "(%s); qemu.log's sweep lines count such chunks",
+                        (unsigned long long)((at - (uintptr_t)s->host) >> 20), why);
+        }
+        omacvm_sweep_add_hold(s, get_clock() - start);
+        return;
+    }
+    before = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+    kr = mach_vm_remap(mach_task_self(), &to, len, 0,
+                       VM_FLAGS_FIXED | VM_FLAGS_OVERWRITE, mach_task_self(), at,
+                       FALSE, &cur, &max, inherit);
+    if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS || to != at ||
+        (cur & (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE)) != (VM_PROT_READ | VM_PROT_WRITE)) {
+        if (!omacvm_sweep_same(at, len, omacvm_sweep_runs, n, why, sizeof(why))) {
+            error_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: a failed remap (%s) changed QEMU's view "
+                         "of guest RAM at +%llu MB (%s): QEMU stops before it reads or "
+                         "writes memory that is not the guest's", mach_error_string(kr),
+                         (unsigned long long)((at - (uintptr_t)s->host) >> 20), why);
+            abort();
+        }
+        snprintf(stop, sizeof(stop), "a remap at +%llu MB failed (%s, protection %d)",
+                 (unsigned long long)((at - (uintptr_t)s->host) >> 20),
+                 mach_error_string(kr), kr == KERN_SUCCESS ? cur : 0);
+        omacvm_sweep_add_hold(s, get_clock() - start);
+        omacvm_sweep_stop(s, stop);
+        return;
+    }
+    if (s->first && !omacvm_sweep_same(at, len, omacvm_sweep_runs, n, why, sizeof(why))) {
+        error_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep: after a remap QEMU's view of guest RAM at "
+                     "+%llu MB maps other memory than the guest's (%s): QEMU stops "
+                     "before it reads or writes there",
+                     (unsigned long long)((at - (uintptr_t)s->host) >> 20), why);
+        abort();
+    }
+    after = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+    s->hour.chunks++;
+    s->run.chunks++;
+    if (before > after) {
+        s->hour.less += before - after;
+        s->run.less += before - after;
+    }
+    omacvm_sweep_add_hold(s, get_clock() - start);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_log(const OmacvmSweep *s, const char *when,
+                             const OmacvmSweepStats *t)
+{
+    uint64_t total = 0, need, seen = 0;
+    char left[160] = "", stopped[240] = "";
+    int64_t p99;
+    int step;
+
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS; step++) {
+        total += t->hold[step];
+    }
+    need = total - total / 100;
+    for (step = 0; step < OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEPS - 1; step++) {
+        seen += t->hold[step];
+        if (seen >= need) {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    p99 = MIN((int64_t)(step + 1) * OMACVM_RECLAIM_STEP_NS, t->longest_ns);
+    if (t->left) {
+        snprintf(left, sizeof(left), "; %" PRIu64 " chunks (%.0f MB) left as they were "
+                 "(not shared with the guest as QEMU's view must be)", t->left,
+                 t->left_bytes / 1048576.0);
+    }
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        snprintf(stopped, sizeof(stopped), "; stopped: %s", s->why);
+    }
+    info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep %s: %" PRIu64 " passes over %.0f MB of guest "
+                "RAM, %" PRIu64 " skipped (QEMU's footprint grew less than 64 MB), %"
+                PRIu64 " chunks remapped; Activity Monitor %.0f MB less; main lock per "
+                "chunk p99 %.2f ms, longest %.2f ms%s%s", when, t->passes,
+                s->size / 1048576.0, t->idle, t->chunks, t->less / 1048576.0,
+                p99 / 1e6, t->longest_ns / 1e6, left, stopped);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_setup(OmacvmSweep *s, void *host, uint64_t size,
+                               int64_t period_s, bool check, int64_t now)
+{
+    memset(s, 0, sizeof(*s));
+    s->host = host;
+    s->size = size;
+    s->at = size;
+    s->first = true;
+    s->check = check;
+    s->period_ns = period_s * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND;
+    s->next_ns = MIN(period_s, OMACVM_SWEEP_FIRST_S) * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND;
+    s->hour_start = now;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Under the BQL, from the sweep's timer: the next chunk of a pass, or the
+ * start of one, and the hour's line. usable: main RAM is still QEMU's
+ * private memory (no dirty logging). Returns when to come again (ns from
+ * now), or -1: stopped for the run.
+ */
+static int64_t omacvm_sweep_step(OmacvmSweep *s, int64_t now, bool usable)
+{
+    uint64_t fp;
+
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    if (now - s->hour_start >= 3600 * NANOSECONDS_PER_SECOND) {
+        omacvm_sweep_log(s, "in the last hour", &s->hour);
+        memset(&s->hour, 0, sizeof(s->hour));
+        s->hour_start = now;
+    }
+    if (!usable) {
+        s->at = s->size;                /* this pass ends here */
+        return s->period_ns;
+    }
+    if (s->at >= s->size) {
+        fp = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+        if (s->footprint_after && fp < s->footprint_after + OMACVM_SWEEP_GROWTH &&
+            s->skipped < OMACVM_SWEEP_SKIPS) {
+            s->skipped++;
+            s->hour.idle++;
+            s->run.idle++;
+            return s->period_ns;
+        }
+        s->skipped = 0;
+        s->at = 0;
+    }
+    omacvm_sweep_chunk(s);
+    if (s->stopped) {
+        return -1;
+    }
+    if (s->at < s->size) {
+        return OMACVM_SWEEP_GAP_NS;
+    }
+    s->first = false;
+    s->hour.passes++;
+    s->run.passes++;
+    s->footprint_after = omacvm_sweep_footprint();
+    if (s->check) {
+        info_report("OmacVM: own-view sweep check: pass %" PRIu64 " done, %" PRIu64
+                    " chunks remapped this run, Activity Monitor %.0f MB less this run, "
+                    "longest chunk %.2f ms, footprint now %.0f MB", s->run.passes,
+                    s->run.chunks, s->run.less / 1048576.0, s->run.longest_ns / 1e6,
+                    s->footprint_after / 1048576.0);
+    }
+    return s->period_ns;
+}
+/* omacvm-sweep: end */
+
+/* The sweep's QEMU side: its timer on the main loop (under the BQL), from the machine's start. */
+static OmacvmSweep omacvm_sweep;
+static QEMUTimer *omacvm_sweep_timer;
+static Notifier omacvm_sweep_init, omacvm_sweep_exit;
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_tick(void *opaque)
+{
+    MemoryRegion *mr = current_machine->ram;
+    int64_t next;
+
+    assert(bql_locked());
+    next = omacvm_sweep_step(&omacvm_sweep, get_clock(), omacvm_ram_private(mr));
+    if (next >= 0) {
+        timer_mod(omacvm_sweep_timer, qemu_clock_get_ns(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME) + next);
+    }
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_at_exit(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    omacvm_sweep_log(&omacvm_sweep, "this run", &omacvm_sweep.run);
+}
+
+static void omacvm_sweep_start(Notifier *n, void *data)
+{
+    MemoryRegion *mr = current_machine ? current_machine->ram : NULL;
+    const char *check = getenv("OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP_CHECK");
+    int64_t period = omacvm_sweep_period(getenv("OMACVM_DCOUNT_SWEEP"));
+
